# Layout rules (workbench only)

When the user references **layout rules**, follow this document exactly. Do not improvise layout "improvements."

**Check List (CL) layout is separate.** Never apply these workbench rules to checklist mode (`mode !== "workbench"`). See `.cursor/rules/checklist-layout-guard.mdc`.

## Workbench table — mandatory constraints

1. **Table width:** stay `w-full` (`table-fixed`). Never switch to `w-max` or shrink-to-content unless the user explicitly asks.
2. **No compact mode:** do not add `wbCellCompact`, `overflow-hidden` on cells, `px-0.5` hacks, or `wbSelectRowCompact` unless the user explicitly asks.
3. **Column changes:** only change `<colgroup>` widths (and `WB_TABLE_COLS` / spacer cells if column count changes). Do not change unrelated cell classes, SKU column, description, loads, etc. unless listed in the task.
4. **Reclaimed width:** any width removed from a column is added to the **right spacer column** (20th column). Keep `WB_TABLE_COLS = 20`. Every row type must include the spacer cell (or `colSpan={WB_TABLE_COLS}` for full-width rows).
5. **Narrowing rule:** when asked to reduce a column by 30%, new width = previous width × 0.7 (round to 2 decimals in `rem`).
6. **List changes:** after editing, list every `<col>` width you changed and the new spacer width.

